{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems","id":92979,"title":"Spotted this comment by Rich re:- testing systems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-17T14:29:16-07:00","id":92979,"title":"Spotted this comment by Rich re:- testing systems","content":"In last week's monday meeting update comment thread Rich mentioned:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Re: Scion- Just discussed the System with both Joltin\u2019 Joe Carriker and Ian \u201cDr\u201d Watson, and we\u2019re all in agreement that we want neither Scion nor Trinity to launch with a surprise system. Our plan is to do internal tests and critiques of the new system and then put it up for community feedback. Not before mid-May, though.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I have to say, that kind of crowd-sourced testing really appeals to me and I'm not that fussed about game mechanics generally speaking. Could be fun to see how things are shaping up on the new systems when the time is right / 'tis ready to unleash <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T06:23:09-07:00","id":93430,"title":"","content":"I thought what they did with DtD was hugely successful, so I definitely hope they will do something similar with the new system for Scion/Trinity. Looking forward to giving it a whirl!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/635-slaunyeh","name":"Slaunyeh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T07:00:54-07:00","id":93460,"title":"","content":"This should be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T05:39:10-07:00","id":94214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=93460#post93460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This should be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's fun to write so far. Last night we had a big design meeting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T07:06:14-07:00","id":94244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=94214#post94214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's fun to write so far. Last night we had a big design meeting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's good that it's all being hashed out! Because this is the whole basic system that everything from Psi modes to Quantum powers to Knacks has to ground itself in and alter. I trust you guys can make it work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T07:54:32-07:00","id":94253,"title":"","content":"Wow, we could be looking at the system as early as two months from now?<br /> <br /> Seriously, are Trinity and Scion coming along MUCH faster than Exalted 3E is? I'm not going to ask for a release date or anything, but I'm curious how these two projects seem to be moving so fast compared to Ex3, which has been delayed upwards of a year already.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are miles yet to go, but it sounds like they're just chuggin' right along here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T09:39:06-07:00","id":94305,"title":"","content":"IMO, I think that Scion and Aeoniverse are advancing faster is because of a few reasons. The first being that the Exalted 2nd edition is pretty broken as it is and so they have a lot of work to do to fix it. Since the Aeoniverse gaming lines were not as broken, then this makes it easier to &quot;fix&quot; and to update.<br /> I also think that they are focusing in on getting every last detail right for Exalted since that is where their largest fanbase is. This was proved by the rousing success of their Exalted Kickstarter. So they do not want to dissappoint the fans that contributed so much money.<br /> Lastly, they also promised a lot on that Kickstarter so they need to produce a lot of material for that launch.<br /> I could be wrong on any of these as I have not been sleeping well as of late, but that is what I think. Hence, my prefacing it with stating &quot;In My Opinion.&quot; <br /> :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T11:36:27-07:00","id":94351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=94253#post94253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, are Trinity and Scion coming along MUCH faster than Exalted 3E is?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they have already been at this a while now officially. Arguably, Ian's had ideas bubbling away for <i><b>years</b></i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> See the (subject to change) schedule page right here: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/</a>. The Aeon reboot is scribbled in for Nov this year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T11:47:19-07:00","id":94361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=94351#post94351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they have already been at this a while now officially. Arguably, Ian's had ideas bubbling away for <i><b>years</b></i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> See the (subject to change) schedule page right here: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/</a>. The Aeon reboot is scribbled in for Nov this year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweetness!<br /> <br /> Obviously, we shouldn't put too much stock in that estimate, but damn it's good to know I may not have to wait that much longer to get my hands on both of these new lines!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T00:04:00-07:00","id":94747,"title":"","content":"To be fair, John and Holden have been considering Ex3 for a long time as well.<br /> <br /> Ignoring the &quot;creating a new system&quot; aspect, for the most part our powers are all standalone, like most of the Storytelling games. At worst, you may have to consider how a defensive power interacts with an offensive power.<br /> <br /> With Exalted, every single power may potentially interlock with numerous other powers, skills, and attributes, so every single power needs to be carefully considered a part of a whole. They're also looking forward to make sure that the foundation they're laying with the core rulebook will interact appropriately with the mechanics they're planning for other Exalts: Dragon-Blooded, Lunars, Abyssals, Infernals, Geitimians, Liminals, etc. etc. etc. It's a massive undertaking and they drastically underestimated the amount of work involved. Like me, they're both pretty new to the development gig.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T04:36:52-07:00","id":94846,"title":"","content":"Ah, yes. I hadn't thought about it quite like that.<br /> <br /> Yeah, in a lot of ways Exalted is a much larger and more complex project. Different splats with different powers, all of which need to be balanced so one splat doesn't suck while another one dominates every other splat. Powers all blend together. Plus the sheer scope and scale of Creation and all the different lands and locales and peoples to design......yeah, suddenly it doesn't all seem quite as easy as I may have made it out to look.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, Scion and Trinity's powers are all largely the same and work largely the same way, and I imagine you don't need to spend quite as much time on world-building and splat design.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, this just goes to show why people who don't actually know how to do something shouldn't criticize the people who do. Now, I wasn't really criticizing, I was just amazed that these two games are moving along so well, whilst Ex3, which I've been following for over a year, is still bogged down in development. Either way, this is a lesson for us all.<br /> <br /> Thanks for giving me some perspective, Ian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T05:58:00-07:00","id":94878,"title":"","content":"There's a great deal of complexity in what we're doing. Trinity's Talents interact with the system largely as Ian indicated, but the Aberrant powerset is going to be *at least* as complex as a full-bore Charmset, with as many hooks and moving parts as the system itself. We've had to consider how to do Talents in concert with novas and noetics (and their baby versions, stalwarts and mesmerists) while keeping the three on a balanced and scaled system. Scions themselves encompass three distinct tiers of power; we think of that when we consider their miracles too, which work far differently than the Gifts of Talents. Each pantheon has to work faithfully according to their myth, and believe me when I say it's a headache to ponder. But Scions needn't be balanced against Aberrants, and we have teams working on both games. It's apples and oranges; just because Exalted's bigger doesn't mean it's more complex, and all three games are gigantic. They're on different systems, as you'll (hopefully) see soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T06:49:39-07:00","id":94901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=94878#post94878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a great deal of complexity in what we're doing. Trinity's Talents interact with the system largely as Ian indicated, but the Aberrant powerset is going to be *at least* as complex as a full-bore Charmset, with as many hooks and moving parts as the system itself. We've had to consider how to do Talents in concert with novas and noetics (and their baby versions, stalwarts and mesmerists) while keeping the three on a balanced and scaled system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not understand a single word of that, but it sounds awesome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T10:01:49-07:00","id":95011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=94901#post94901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I did not understand a single word of that, but it sounds awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div> As a rough don't quote me analogy: we have to design two games. One that balances enlightened mortals, Dragon-Blooded, and Solars, and another game that follows Alchemicals from Exaltation to the end of their Essence span. Thankfully, we don't have to balance these games against one another. We're designing a system that allows us to do both and more. You dig?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T12:42:57-07:00","id":95145,"title":"","content":"For the most part, yeah. I've never encountered the Trinity Continuum and Scion is probably not the best frame of reference in this context, so I'm mostly waiting for the dev blog or the Kickstarter or whatever to get a more concrete sense of how Trinity Continuum powers actually work in a gameplay sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T13:57:16-07:00","id":95193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=95145#post95145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the most part, yeah. I've never encountered the Trinity Continuum and Scion is probably not the best frame of reference in this context, so I'm mostly waiting for the dev blog or the Kickstarter or whatever to get a more concrete sense of how Trinity Continuum powers actually work in a gameplay sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noone (outside the devs) have encountered the <b><i>Continuum</i></b>. <br /> <br /> The Trinity Continuum is 'new', the Trinity RPG (previously 'Aeon') is the original game in what became the Trinity <i><b>Universe</b></i> and is readily available here for under $10: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3407/Trinity-Rulebook?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...-Rulebook?it=1</a><br /> <br /> Why wait just for the Kickstarter on the reboot, as you can get some Trinity goodness right now and enjoy the reboot later when it arrives <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T14:20:25-07:00","id":95204,"title":"","content":"If we're gonna plug, I'd also strongly suggest picking up Adventure! from the same place:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/5/Adventure-Rulebook?it=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/5.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/5/Adventure-Rulebook?it=1\" target=\"_blank\"> Adventure! Tales of the Aeon Society Rulebook - Onyx Path Publishing | Trinity Universe | Trinity Universe | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/5/Adventure-Rulebook?it=1\" target=\"_blank\"> http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/5/Adventure-Rulebook?it=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Adventure! Tales of the Aeon Society Rulebook - The Dawn of a New Age In 1922, a new era begins. An era of excitement and imagination. An era when men are forthright an </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One of the best single-book games and purchases I've ever made. So much fun with that game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T08:00:04-07:00","id":95634,"title":"","content":"Is team Trinity using any of the Exalted core engine work? Just curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T08:43:35-07:00","id":95672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=95634#post95634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is team Trinity using any of the Exalted core engine work? Just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div> No. Several of us are Exalted veterans, and one member of the engine team also worked on 3e, but Exalted 3e is built off a core of Storyteller. Trinity doesn't use Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:00:20-07:00","id":95882,"title":"","content":"Ditching Storyteller entirely? Whoa. ...I hate to say this, but that's probably for the best. Spinning off d20, like M&amp;M did?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:17:48-07:00","id":95903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=95882#post95882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ditching Storyteller entirely? Whoa. ...I hate to say this, but that's probably for the best. Spinning off d20, like M&amp;M did?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still uses dicepools of d10s, like Storyteller/Storytelling, according to Ian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T15:13:34-07:00","id":95978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=95903#post95903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still uses dicepools of d10s, like Storyteller/Storytelling, according to Ian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. As long as it works. I'm curious how it will be not-Storyteller now. I won't be able to shell out for a physical copy (I did so for Mage 20, and that's pretty much all I can manage for a while), but as someone who owns all three Aeon games (I own a copy of Aeon that <i>actually has Aeon</i> in the title), I'm going to <i>have</i> to participate in the inevitable Kickstarter. With an ID like mine, how can I not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T15:37:43-07:00","id":95998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=95978#post95978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. As long as it works. I'm curious how it will be not-Storyteller now. I won't be able to shell out for a physical copy (I did so for Mage 20, and that's pretty much all I can manage for a while), but as someone who owns all three Aeon games (I own a copy of Aeon that <i>actually has Aeon</i> in the title), I'm going to <i>have</i> to participate in the inevitable Kickstarter. With an ID like mine, how can I not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, with the good ol' black plastic cover? I picked up mine for $20 at a Hastings years ago. I had no idea what I was getting into.<br /> <br /> In a GOOD way, of course!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T19:44:56-07:00","id":96137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=95672#post95672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No. Several of us are Exalted veterans, and one member of the engine team also worked on 3e, but Exalted 3e is built off a core of Storyteller. Trinity doesn't use Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, very interesting. So how is the development coming along? Any idea when we might start seeing previews? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T02:05:40-07:00","id":96249,"title":"","content":"Hopefully it's nothing too exotic. So long as it retains the same flexibility I'm happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T16:14:34-07:00","id":96571,"title":"","content":"My memory may be letting me down on this, but I'm pretty sure I saw Ian mention somewhere (um... rpg.net maybe?) that while the new Continuum rules are not strictly Storyteller/Storytelling system, its essentially an evolution of that. d10's, dots etc. If that's the case there will be plenty that looks familiar I'd imagine, but enough change to tackle things like game balance, scaling, ironing out power issues (Abberant, lookin' at you). If I get time I'll see if I can track down the thread, it was a little while ago...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T16:09:23-07:00","id":97106,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping for not too much change in Aberrant. Aberrant was high power, but that was a good thing, and I'm glad an RPG decided to explore that space. If anything, Aeon needed to be bumped up. The last thing I want is to see Aberrant neutered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T16:14:29-07:00","id":97110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=96571#post96571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My memory may be letting me down on this, but I'm pretty sure I saw Ian mention somewhere (um... rpg.net maybe?) that while the new Continuum rules are not strictly Storyteller/Storytelling system, its essentially an evolution of that. d10's, dots etc. If that's the case there will be plenty that looks familiar I'd imagine, but enough change to tackle things like game balance, scaling, ironing out power issues (Abberant, lookin' at you). If I get time I'll see if I can track down the thread, it was a little while ago...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because we own Scion and Trinity, rather than licensing them from CCP, we're making our game system for them rather than use Storyteller (like cWoD and Exalted) or Storytelling (like nWoD).<br /> <br /> It's a d10 dice pool system. The character sheet has dots. That's about all we've said, apart from the fact as stated last GenCon that as it's the system for Scion and Trinity, it needs to do power scaling, as it has to handle everything from an Adventure! Daredevil to a Scion God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T16:30:10-07:00","id":97117,"title":"","content":"I'd rather be a Nova with my own universe than a Scion God -- personally. PLANCK SCALING!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T07:23:03-07:00","id":97502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=97110#post97110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because we own Scion and Trinity, rather than licensing them from CCP, we're making our game system for them rather than use Storyteller (like cWoD and Exalted) or Storytelling (like nWoD). It's a d10 dice pool system. The character sheet has dots. That's about all we've said, apart from the fact as stated last GenCon that as it's the system for Scion and Trinity, it needs to do power scaling, as it has to handle everything from an Adventure! Daredevil to a Scion God.</div> </div> </div> </div>There you go then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T07:43:21-07:00","id":97514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=97117#post97117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather be a Nova with my own universe than a Scion God -- personally. PLANCK SCALING!</div> </div> </div> </div> The cosmologies are pretty radically different (and frankly irreconcilable). However, there's a lot of nova powers that need to be addressed in light of a continuum cosmology that includes quanta, psi and telluric energies of the hollow earth rather than a separate game line where it's quantum \u00fcber alles - time travel is one of them, Planck scaling another, telepathy, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T08:22:07-07:00","id":97531,"title":"","content":"It will certainly be wonderful to have a system that more perfectly captures all of that. A lot of us are excited and elated to hear the news that Trinity Continuum is on the horizon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T08:23:47-07:00","id":97534,"title":"","content":"Are any of you devs mathematicians?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2239-lyre","name":"lyre","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:47:33-07:00","id":100495,"title":"","content":"As long as Aberrant continues to capture the 'quantum gods' thing that drew me in to begin with, I'm good to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T21:16:03-07:00","id":103132,"title":"","content":"News like this is always really exciting for me. I know my group would jump at opportunities to playtest Scion stuff. Despite the mechanical train wreck of the game we have never failed to have loads of fun playing it with working mechanics we could really get into it, Trinity stuff is pretty exciting too, but my group isn't at all familiar with it, We love super heros, but it's hard to tell how they would react to abberent as we normally only play with Marvel as a setting. I'll just keep hoping that Daredevils get expanded on further and developed in the other time periods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T12:59:17-07:00","id":104277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=97110#post97110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because we own Scion and Trinity, rather than licensing them from CCP, we're making our game system for them rather than use Storyteller (like cWoD and Exalted) or Storytelling (like nWoD).<br /> <br /> It's a d10 dice pool system. The character sheet has dots. That's about all we've said, apart from the fact as stated last GenCon that as it's the system for Scion and Trinity, it needs to do power scaling, as it has to handle everything from an Adventure! Daredevil to a Scion God.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scaling is probably the number one issue to deal with, so I hope you folks find an elegant solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T11:27:47-07:00","id":109480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/92979-spotted-this-comment-by-rich-re-testing-systems?p=104277#post104277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Scaling is probably the number one issue to deal with, so I hope you folks find an elegant solution.</div> </div> </div> </div> We actually found four, one of which is setting-specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg